# motoquencer `constantlength` on a `linktonext` chain.
#
# A linked member has no range and no play order of its own — "the current step
# number of the linked sequencer will always be the same as the step number of the
# main sequencer" (motoquencer.md:946) — so when `fadermode = 13` puts the MEMBER's
# repeats lane on the faders, the compensation there is scoped by the MAIN's
# start/end range, exactly like every other consumer of the range.
#
# SPEC-GAP (documented in seqcore.hpp): the level itself is read off the chain
# main too. The Forge's own MFPS generator wires `constantlength` on a track's
# main lane only and leaves the linked lanes without it, so reading each
# instance's own input would leave the member lanes silently uncompensated.
#
# The main's `endstep = 3` keeps step 4 out of the range. Editing the member's
# step 1 from 1 to 3 repeats is paid for by the member's step 3 (4 -> 2); the
# member's step 4 keeps its 8 repeats.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock          = I1
    fadermode      = I2
    constantlength = I3
    endstep        = 3
    numsteps       = 4
    numfaders      = 4
    linktonext     = 1
    cv             = O1
[motoquencer]
    cv             = O2
>>>
# fadermode 13 = the linked member's repeats lane (10 per chain instance + 3)
@2 set I2 13
# with the feature off: member step 3 -> 4 repeats, member step 4 -> 8
@3 move F3 0.2
@4 move F4 0.4666667
@4 expect F4 0.4666667 tol 1e-4
@5 set I3 1
# member step 1: 1 -> 3 repeats. Step 2 is at the floor, step 3 pays the +2, and
# step 4 — outside the MAIN's range — is left alone.
@6 move F1 0.1333333
@6 expect F1 0.1333333 tol 1e-4
@6 expect F2 0 tol 1e-4
@6 expect F3 0.0666667 tol 1e-4
@6 expect F4 0.4666667 tol 1e-4
